x86_64-linux  cxx1 answers [except.spec]/9 by calling `abort` where the escape is certain; clang calls its own guard, `__clang_call_terminate`, which calls `_ZSt9terminatev`. Measured on this case: clang's assembly names both of those and neither `abort` nor a resume, and this suite excludes both of clang's by name - see the `-fexceptions` note in tools/mangled-names - so what is left is one cxx1-only `abort`. The `_Unwind_Resume` beside it is the same difference one step further out: cxx1 reaches its abort through the cleanup path the function already has, and clang's terminate guard needs none.
x86_64-windows  The same one name, without the resume: this target has no call-site list to reach the abort through, so `abort` is the whole of the difference. clang's `__clang_call_terminate` and `_ZSt9terminatev` are excluded by this suite; cxx1's `abort` is not, and there is nothing to exclude it by that would not also hide a real one.
arm64-darwin  The same as x86_64-linux with Mach-O's leading underscore - `_abort` and `__Unwind_Resume` against clang's excluded terminate guard. Every other name in the case agrees.
